Description: Tetun (Tetum) locale and language resources for Edukasaun OS
 Tetun (ISO 639 code "tet") is the national language of Timor-Leste and the
 local language of Edukasaun OS. This package provides:
  * the tet_TL.UTF-8 glibc locale, compiled on the target system;
  * original community gettext and Qt catalogs (432 draft terms);
  * a complete draft translation of LXQt and its applications (panel,
    settings, session, PCManFM-Qt, QTerminal, LXImage-Qt, ...) and Openbox;
  * partial native catalogs for GTK 2/3/4, GNOME Shell, Cinnamon, Nemo,
    Xfce, Thunar, MATE, Caja, LXDE, PCManFM and Dolphin;
  * the eduka-tet tool to enable or disable Tetun per user, reversibly.
 .
 LXQt shows the Tetun catalogs only with the loader patches shipped in
 /usr/share/doc/eduka-language-pack-tet/lxqt-patches. Orthography targets INL
 conventions but has not been approved by INL.
